assessment.verification_assessment:
Acceptance is observable through five named material failure classes:
- no collapse past VERIFY on producer success;
- distinct verifier evaluates the exact candidate, with rejection→IMPLEMENT under budget;
- canonical REVIEW/ACCEPT with actual closure receipts only;
- missing, duplicate, stale or miscorrelated evidence holds despite process success;
- shared WorkerProvider boundary with no test shortcut or sidecar owner.

Each class admits one discriminating negative control exercised through the production composition path, plus architecture checks and a terminal full regression. One independent verifier verdict on the exact candidate SHA is meaningful because the classes all concern a single lifecycle path. Explicit non-claims exclude live/shared-profile activation, which keeps the verdict scoped to local proof. Two caveats: the acceptance criterion restates the scope text rather than listing checks, so the failure-class list must serve as the operative predicate; and dependency DONE status is reported, not independently verified here.
